## Building with this design system

Proliferate's UI is a **Tailwind-v4 preset** system: components carry their
own styling, and you compose layout with utility classes. Two rules matter
more than everything else below.

### 1. The stock Tailwind palette and type ramp DO NOT EXIST here

The token authority opens with `--color-*: initial; --text-*: initial`,
which **erases** Tailwind's built-in colours and text sizes. So `text-sm`,
`text-2xl`, `text-base`, `bg-slate-500`, `text-gray-400` and every other
stock colour/size class resolve to **nothing** — no error, just unstyled
output.

Use the semantic roles instead. Colours (the ones the system actually
leans on, most-used first):

| Role | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| `text-foreground` / `text-muted-foreground` / `text-faint` | primary / secondary / tertiary text |
| `text-destructive`, `text-success`, `text-warning` | status text |
| `bg-background` | the page surface |
| `bg-surface`, `bg-surface-elevated`, `bg-surface-elevated-secondary`, `bg-surface-control` | raised surfaces, in ascending elevation |
| `bg-card`, `bg-popover` | card and popover surfaces |
| `bg-hover`, `bg-active`, `bg-selected` | interaction states |
| `border-border`, `border-border-light`, `border-border-heavy`, `border-input` | dividers and control outlines |
| `bg-primary` / `text-primary-foreground` | the primary action pair |
| `text-sidebar-foreground`, `text-sidebar-muted-foreground`, `bg-sidebar-background` | sidebar-scoped roles |

Type — these __DS_TEXT_ROLE_COUNT__ named scales are the entire ramp (each
carries its own size, line-height and letter-spacing):

__DS_TEXT_ROLES_LIST__

`text-ui-sm` and `text-ui` are the workhorses for interface text;
`text-body` for prose; `text-heading` / `text-title` for section and page
headings.

Everything non-colour, non-type is ordinary Tailwind and works normally:
`flex`, `grid`, `gap-4`, `p-6`, `w-full`, `rounded-lg`, `items-center`.
Icon sizing has named helpers: `icon-tight`, `icon-paired`, `icon-status`.

### 2. It is dark-first, and needs no provider

There is **no ThemeProvider and no ColorModeProvider** — tokens live on
`:root` in CSS, so components are correctly styled as soon as the
stylesheet is loaded. Just render them:

```jsx
<Button size="sm">Create workspace</Button>
```

Dark is the default. For light, set `data-mode="light"` on the root
element (`<html data-mode="light">`); every token flips.

Two components need a wrapper: `tooltip-primitive`'s raw parts (`Tooltip`,
`TooltipTrigger`, `TooltipContent`) must sit inside a `TooltipProvider`
exported from that same module — the styled `Tooltip` primitive wraps this
internally and needs neither. `ToastHost` is the single toast mount: render
it once near the app root, then raise toasts through `showToast`.

### 3. Where the truth lives

Read `styles.css` and its `@import` closure (the compiled tokens and
utilities) first. For any one component, its own
`components/<group>/<Name>/<Name>.prompt.md` has the purpose, the import
line, and the `Demo` story; `<Name>.jsx` is that component's real, current
source — types stripped, JSX left intact — copied straight from the
registry this payload was built from.

This is a **library-only sync**: every card here is one `#product/...`
component with a self-contained registry demo. There are no page or
surface cards (workspace shells, settings panes assembled from these
parts, chat surfaces) — composition, anatomy, and "which pattern owns this
skeleton" rules live in the source repo's `specs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` (the
"Component Library" section), not in this payload.

### 4. An idiomatic composition

Library components for the controls, DS utilities for your own glue:

```jsx
<div className="flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface-elevated p-6">
  <div className="flex items-center justify-between">
    <h2 className="text-heading text-foreground">Cloud workspace</h2>
    <Badge tone="success">Ready</Badge>
  </div>
  <p className="text-ui-sm text-muted-foreground">
    Runs on a managed sandbox. Commits push to your branch.
  </p>
  <div className="flex items-center gap-2">
    <Button size="sm">Open</Button>
    <Button size="sm" variant="secondary">Settings</Button>
  </div>
</div>
```

# ProliferateUI (library-registry@__DS_GIT_SHA__)

This design system is built directly from the live `product-client`
component registry — every one of the __DS_COMPONENT_COUNT__ components
below is real, current, in-repo source, not a published package snapshot.

## Where things are

- `_ds_bundle.js` — the whole-library bundle at the project root; loads
  every component onto `window.ProliferateUI`, plus `__demos` (entry name
  → demo component) and `__tiers` (the registry's own tier/group listing).
  First line is a `/* @ds-bundle: … */` metadata header.
- `styles.css` — the single stylesheet entry: it `@import`s the fonts and
  the compiled component styles (`_ds_bundle.css`). Link this one file.
- `components/<group>/<Name>/<Name>.prompt.md` (purpose, import line,
  story list), `<Name>.jsx` (real source), `<Name>.html` (the rendered
  variant card).
- `fonts/` — `@font-face` files + `fonts.css`.

For a specific component, `read_file("components/<group>/<Name>/<Name>.prompt.md")`.

## Loading

Add these two lines to your page once (React must be on the page first):

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
<script src="_ds_bundle.js"></script>
```

Components are then available at `window.ProliferateUI.*`. Mount into a
dedicated child node (e.g. `<div id="ds-root">`), not the host page's own
React root, so the two trees don't collide:

```jsx
const { Button } = window.ProliferateUI;
ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById('ds-root')).render(<Button size="sm">Open</Button>);
```

